<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's 1997 energy demand seen up 7.2 pct - govt.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's 1997 energy demand seen up 7.2 pct - govt.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand is expected to rise 7.2 percent to 176.97 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) this year from an estimated 165.02 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement the nation's 1997 energy imports were expected to reach $27.5 billion and exports $5.5 billion.</p>
<p>Oil products consumption growth was expected to lag due to an industrial slowdown and a decline in demand from the power generation sector, it said.</p>
<p>Liquefied natural gas (LNG) consumption is forecast to rise sharply on growing use of home fuel and hydroelectric power, the ministry said.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of South Korea's demand forecast for energy resources in 1997, compared with 1996. (Figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage, 1996 figures are preliminary):</p>
<p>				1997		    1996</p>
<p>				Amount		  Amount</p>
<p> Total		     176,972   (7.2)     165,016   (9.7)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    760,700   (5.5)     721,041   (6.5)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			  12,024  (29.2)	 9,309  (31.4)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Hard coal		   4,831  (-7.9)	 5,245 (-16.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	  48,629   (8.5)	44,811  (17.6)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	    75,862   (2.6)	73,924  (10.3)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power     6,044  (16.2)	 5,202  (-5.0)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Other			 1,344  (15.8)	 1,161  (10.5)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p>(Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy).</p>
